# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/raw/ is INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored.
#
# The pinned FAOSTAT + World Bank snapshot (a few MB, manifest + checksummed)
# is the one thing that must survive a fresh clone: FAOSTAT revises its bulk
# file in place with no version number, so "download fresh and hope" is not
# reproducible. Everything downstream of data/raw/ regenerates deterministically
# from it via `python scripts/run_pipeline.py`, so only the downstream
# artifacts are ignored below.
#
# The one exception: the FAOSTAT bulk CSV is committed as the ~2 MB zip it
# ships as. Its ~50 MB extracted form is a build artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/**/Food_Security_Data_E_All_Data_Normalized/

# --- regenerable data/model artifacts (reproduced by scripts/run_pipeline.py) ---
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
!data/interim/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
models/*
!models/.gitkeep

# --- generated reports (figures/metrics regenerate on every run) ---
reports/figures/*.png
reports/metrics/*.json
reports/book_figures/
!reports/figures/.gitkeep
!reports/metrics/.gitkeep

# --- generated UI data contract (the one file dashboard_export.py writes) ---
site/agrisentinel_data.js

# --- notebook execution artifacts (outputs are useful in git; caches are not) ---
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
env/

# --- Node ---
node_modules/

# --- coursework drafts and exports (the final report lives in docs/) ---
*.pptx
/*.docx
/*.pdf
~$*

# --- tooling / IDE / OS ---
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
